stringFiles[85].addEntry("access_fee", "This ability allows you to place an access fee on any public building you own.  Entry to a building with an access fee set is restricted to players who have paid the fee.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("accuse", "/accuse: You point accusingly at everyone else./accuse self: Have you been bad? Tsk, tsk./accuse target: You point accusingly at (target name).");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("ache", "/ache: You ache all over./ache self: Eat something bad? Your stomach grumbles and aches./ache target: You let (target name) know that your body aches for (him, her, or it).");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("actionshot1", "/actionshot1 <target>: This ranged attack can wreak havoc with a target's Action pool drain and regeneration rates.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("actionshot2", "/actionshot2 <target>: This area ranged attack can wreak havoc with a target's Action pool drain and regeneration rates.  This is more powerful than Action Shot 1.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("activateclone", "This command is used to activate a clone and send the user to the nearest Cloning Facility after death.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("adjust", "/adjust: You adjust your outfit. There you go. Perfect!/adjust self: You tighten down your gear and get ready for action./adjust target: You adjust (target name)'s outfit for (him, her, or it).");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("adn", "/adn: You openly show that your patience has expired./adn self: A bit frustrated with yourself?/adn target: You encourage (target name) to hurry. Any day now!");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("ad_fees_1", "The merchant gains a reduction in the cost of maintaining a vendor registered on the planetary map.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("afk", "/afk: You notify everyone around you that you are going AFK. Hurry back, now!/afk self: OK... You are really AFK now./afk target: You point out that (target name) is AFK.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("afk4drink", "/afk4drink: We'll be waiting! You announce you are AFK to get a drink./afk4drink self: You let everyone know that you will be going to grab a drink next break./afk4drink target: You remind everyone that (target name) went AFK to go get a beverage.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("afk4food", "/afk4food: Your stomach will thank you.  You announce you are AFK to grab a bite./afk4food self: You announce that you will be AFK to grab some food at the next break in the action./afk4food target: You let everyone know that (target name) went AFK to find sustenance.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("agree", "/agree: You nod in agreement./agree self: You agree with yourself./agree target: You agree with (target name).");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("aim", "/aim: This combat move allows you to give up an attack round in order to gain better accuracy on your next ranged attack.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("airguitar", "/airguiter: You rock the crowd./airguiter self: You rock out./airguiter target: You rock out for (target name).");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("alert", "This command utilizes the alert ability.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("amaze", "/amaze: That was amazing! How did they do that?/amaze self: You amaze yourself!/amaze target: You try to amaze (target name) with a magic trick.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("amazing", "/amazing");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("animalattack", "/animalAttack <target>: This ability allows a Jedi to enter the mind of his or her look-at target and cause it to attack the current combat target. Note that this ability will only work on creatures.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("animalcalm", "/animalCalm <target>: This ability will cause a target that is in combat to stop attacking, returning to its normal peaceful state. Note that this ability will only work on creatures.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("animalscare", "/animalScare <target>: This ability allows a Jedi to enter the mind of the target and fill it with unease, scaring the target away. Note that this ability will only work on creatures.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("anon", "This command allows the user to go anonymous.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("anxious", "/anxious: You feel anxious./anxious self: You look around anxiously./anxious target: You look anxiously at (target name).");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("apologize", "/apologize: OOPS!! Sorry everyone!!/apologize self: You apologize to yourself. But, what good is that going to do unless you forgive yourself too?/apologize target: You apologize to (target name) and beg (his, her, or its) forgiveness.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("applaud", "/applaud: You give a hearty round of applause./applaud self: You give yourself a hand. Go ahead, you deserve it!/applaud target: Bravo! Bravo! You give (target name) an ovation.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("applydisease", "/applydisease <target>: This command will enable you to attack your target with disease, if you have the proper item.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("applypoison", "/applypoison <target>: This command will enable you to attack your target with poison, if you have the proper item.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("arch", "/arch: You arch your back like a cat./arch self: You arch your back in an effort to work the kinks out. SNAP! CRACK! POP!/arch target: You arch your back seductively for (target name).");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("areatrack", "/areatrack: Gives the Ranger the ability to study tracking clues in the area to figure out what kind of creatures or people have been in the region recently.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("areatrack_animal", "Gives the Ranger the ability to scan animal activity using the /areatrack command.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("areatrack_direction", "Gives the Ranger the ability to judge the approximate direction of a target using /areatrack.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("areatrack_distance", "Gives the Ranger the ability to judge the approximate distance of targets in the area using /areatrack.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("areatrack_npc", "Enhances the Ranger's tracking skills to hunt down non-player characters.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("areatrack_player", "Gives the Ranger the ability to track players using /areatrack.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("assist", "/assist <name>: Assist lets you immediately Combat Target somebody else's current target.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("associatedroidcontroldevicewithship", "Associate a droid with a ship, so that it's loaded in your ship when you launch into space.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("astromech_droid_cert_1", "This certification allows you to equip an Astromech with a level 1 data storage module, or a v1 Flight Computer, on your starship.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("astromech_droid_cert_2", "This certification allows you to equip an Astromech with a level 2 data storage module, or a v2 Flight Computer, on your starship.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("astromech_droid_cert_3", "This certification allows you to equip an Astromech with a level 3 data storage module, or a v3 Flight Computer, on your starship.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("astromech_droid_cert_4", "This certification allows you to equip an Astromech with a level 4 datastorage module, or a v4 Flight Computer, on your starship.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("astromech_droid_cert_5", "This certification allows you to equip an Astromech with a level 5 data storage module, or a v5 Flight Computer, on your starship.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("astromech_droid_cert_6", "This certification allows you to equip an Astromech with a level 6 data storage module, or a v6 Flight Computer, on your starship.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("attack", "/attack: This initiates combat against your current target.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("attend", "/attend: You listen hard./attend self: You listen to something only you can hear./attend target: You listen to (target name).");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("avoidincapacitation", "/avoidIncapacitation: This ability allows a Jedi to prevent themselves from going into an unconscious state.  This power only lasts for a short time and can quickly deplete a Jedi of Force power if they try to remain conscious for a lengthy period of time.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("ayt", "/ayt: You try to figure out who is AFK and who is not./ayt self: I don't know.  Are you really here?/ayt target: Hello? (target name)? Well, it seems (his, her, or its) lights are on, but is anyone home?");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("backhand", "/backhand: You raise your hand as if to backhand slap someone./backhand self: You backhand slap your other palm, emphasizing your point./backhand target: You slap (him, her, or it) in the face with a swift backhand.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("bad", "/bad: Uh. What just went horribly wrong?/bad self: Just how bad have you been?/bad target: You make it obvious that you think (target name) has been bad.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("badfeeling", "/badfeeling: You have a bad feeling about this.../badfeeling self: You start to express your bad feeling and think better of it./badfeeling target: You signal to (him, her, or it) that you have a bad feeling about this...");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("bah", "/bah: BAH!/bah self: You take one look at your surroundings and think aloud, BAH!/bah target: You look (target name) up and down and utter, BAH!");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("bak", "/bak: You let everyone know that you are back at your keyboard./bak self: You smile contentedly as you realize you are back to your old self again!/bak target: You wish that (target name) would come back to (his, her, or its) keyboard.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("bandfill", "This ability allows you to plays songs with the Bandfill instrument.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("bang", "/bang: You bang your head to the music./bang self: You bang your head against the wall./bang target: You bang (target name)'s head against the wall.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("bark", "/bark: You get on all fours and bark like a dog./bark self: You bark at yourself./bark target: BARK BARK!  You bark at (target name).");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("bat", "/bat: And just whom are you trying to impress?  You bat your lashes./bat self: You practice batting your lashes./bat target: You bat your lashes at (target name).");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("batlashes", "/batlashes:  And just whom are you trying to impress?   You bat your lashes./batlashes self:  You practice batting your lashes./batlashes target:  You bat your lashes at (target name).");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("battlefieldstatus", "This command allows the user to view a battlefield's status.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("bbl", "/bbl: You tell everyone you will be back later... See ya soon!/bbl self: Trying to have an out of body experience, are we?/bbl target: You let (target name) know that you will be back later.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("beam", "/beam: Feeling radiant, are we?/beam self: You beam at yourself./beam target: You beam at (target name).");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("bearhug", "/bearhug: You hold your arms out wide and look for a target to bear-hug./bearhug self: You bear-hug yourself and stretch out your shoulders./bearhug target: You give (target name) a great, big bear-hug that lifts (him, her, or it) off the ground.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("beckon", "/beckon: You do your best to gather everyone around you./beckon self: You summon your inner strength./beckon target: You motion at (target name) to come here.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("belch", "/belch: You let out a resounding belch! Feel better?/belch self: You try to muffle your belch./belch target: You belch in (target name)'s face.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("berserk1", "/berserk1: While berserk, you cause more melee damage to your targets but get hit more often in return.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("berserk2", "/berserk2: While berserk, you cause more melee damage to your targets but get hit more often in return.  This is more powerful than Berserk 1.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("bet", "After joining a suitable gambling station, you may target the station and use the /bet command to set your wager.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("bite", "/bite: You snap your teeth at everyone around you./bite self: You bite your lip nervously./bite target: You bite (target name) on the leg.");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("blame", "/blame: You blame everyone else./blame self: You blame yourself./blame target: You blame (target name).");
stringFiles[85].addEntry("bleed", "/bleed: MEDIC!!  You bleed on the ground./bleed self: You bleed all over yourself and make a nice pool of blood at your feet./bleed target: You bleed all over (target name).");
