stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_143896d2", "I think that the majority of pilot trainers are registered with the planetary map. Try opening the planetary map with CTRL+V. On the right-hand side is a listing of categories. Look under 'trainer' to find any local pilot teacher who's looking for pupils.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_144ec5cc", "Sounds good. Thanks!");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_148c4dad", "Very well then. Feel free to ask.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_17bc5d9b", "When you approach the space station, use SHIFT+C to target it and open communication with the commander. You will be asked if you want to purchase repairs or if you want to land on the planet.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_2099fa73", "Interesting. Why are you here outside the hangar?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_21bf1a8c", "How do I join the Alliance?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_232bfee8", "Why don't you fly any more?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_270c87b2", "How do I get them to repair my ship?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_27186cee", "I don't have enough money.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_29894b97", "I don't know how to check.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_2cc72ac", "Could I ask some other questions?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_3059f369", "What then?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_32146025", "Then what?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_366f0593", "Oh I will. I do.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_3b435c91", "Greetings. Ah, tell me of your journeys in the great expanses beyond this planet. It has been too long since I last flew such a flight. I long to remember that feeling.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_3c8b5d06", "I enjoy talking to pilots and hearing about their flights. Takes me back to some of my own best memories. Helps me to relive them.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_4626423a", "Greetings and welcome to Theed. I apologize, but I'm looking to speak with pilots and those seeking to become pilots. If you get involved with space flight, I might be able to answer some questions, but otherwise I'm not going to be of much help.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_472f61d1", "Local space stations are the easiest way to get your ship repaired. When you are heading back here, you should stop at the space station and ask them for repairs. They will provide a quick estimate on what it will take to get you back on track.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_495777c0", "Have you checked any vendors? Merchants use vendors to help sell their merchandise. Shipwrights put finished starships and ship components for sale on their vendors, and then you can go to those vendors and purchase what you need.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_52939a0", "How do I check my email?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_558a361a", "The Imperial Navy? I've heard that they are sending out recruitment emails to everyone they can locate these days. Have you checked your email today?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_55c77e3b", "On the lower right-hand side of your screen should be a 'letter' icon that is flashing. Double-click on this icon and it will bring up your personal email. Read over the subject and sender, and scroll through the body text to get all the details.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_5618d2cd", "No. I have received no email.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_5989c487", "There are all sorts of civilian contracts available on the 'mission terminals' you find throughout town. Look for them near any major structure. Use the terminal to bring up the current list of local contracts. Choose the one that interests you most and you'll make money when the task is complete.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_5b893f7c", "It does.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_5cd38acb", "That makes sense. Have fun with that.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_5e410744", "Right-click on the map location to create and activate a waypoint. Follow the waypoint to the trainer's location.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_5ff8baab", "I was wondering if you could answer some questions?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_68cb68ff", "Is there anyone else I could fly for?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_6f0ab63b", "Stay safe, my friend.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_6f5ce457", "That's what I hear. Or something like that anyway. The Empire's pretty well-equipped and can't really have much of a navy if their pilots don't have ships. I've also heard rumors that the Alliance has a fleet of ships for new recruits.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_72df796a", "Good luck with that. I don't want to get too close to the Galactic Civil War, myself.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_73f8df86", "Hey, any time. Anything else?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_82519d76", "Things are tough all over during this Galactic Civil War. A lot of pilots are flying for either the Empire or the Rebellion these days. Ever think of joining the military to get a starship?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_8515e448", "Yes. I have an email from the Imperial Navy.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_8b23fac", "I want to learn to fly.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_8b37a99a", "How do I make money?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_8cf9be64", "Where can I find a vendor?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_8ef8dbfb", "I have another question.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_93280d8a", "Good idea. Thanks!");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_97856fdc", "If I can answer them, I'd be more than happy to do so.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_a463a3c1", "You're welcome. Anything else?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_a8aae630", "[He doesn't say anything, but gestures toward his protocol droid.]");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_a9850aec", "I got an email from the Alliance!");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_abc6d2f6", "Your best bet is to get in touch with the Empire and sign up for their training program. There are others who will urge you to put your efforts to use in the Alliance, but fools will be fools.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_acc368b1", "How do I join the Empire?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_add31f19", "I need a starship.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_b0b2621a", "It doesn't");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_b641cda6", "Where can I find a bazaar terminal?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_b9b27823", "Thank you.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_ba3c26af", "You did? These are desperate times, indeed. The email should probably indicate where you are supposed to go for initial recruitment.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_ba95f774", "Bazaar terminals are located all over major cities. Check the areas surrounding major hot spots like the starport, the bank, any of the cantinas, or even the hospitals.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_c00207b0", "Hello. Hello. You have the look of one seeking adventures in space. Flying is the only part of the job I miss. I was a captain on a freighter, you see. Flew all over the galaxy. Ah, nothing matches being at the helm of a ship flying through the deep, black reaches of space.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_c2db6878", "Good-bye.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_c4682ea6", "Thanks!");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_c9e97ed5", "How else would I join up?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_cb747ceb", "Hmm. Me neither. Maybe you should give it a little time?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_cc7c9754", "Don't mention it. Anything else?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_cdb17e79", "How do I check the planetary map?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_cf5fc0f", "How do I repair my starship?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_d4c6e8cd", "No problem! Anything else?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_d9231b4f", "There are freelance pilots working in most systems. Some are CorSec pilots, others are part of the RSF of Naboo, and of course, others are smugglers or pirates. I wouldn't recommend those last two if you want to pursue a lengthy career, but, at the same time, some of the best military pilots I know were once smugglers. Most freelance organizations will send recruitment emails. You might try checking your email for something like that.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_da08c873", "That's sort of tricky. There may be some Alliance pilots bold enough to register their locations on the planetary map. Have you looked at the planetary map yet?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_e013f498", "Look for the flashing 'envelope' icon on your interface. It's placed on the lower right-hand side of your screen by default.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_e1c13ebb", "Double-click on the envelope icon, and read your mail! Anything else?");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_e6b5489e", "I retired. And I'm pretty happy about it. The only thing I miss is the flying. The rest of it can rot. All the forms and logs to keep track of, safeguarding your cargo, having to deal with bureaucracy and red tape every time you docked at a space station or planetary starport. No thanks. It is the journey I miss, but not the destinations.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_e843e3ab", "Use the command CTRL+V to open the planetary map. On the right side of your display, you will see a listing of trainers by category. All local trainers who register with the planet will appear on this list. Click the 'Trainer' tab and then look for a pilot trainer.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_eab69714", "Strange. Seems that if they undertook the risk to send you a message, they would make it clear how to respond. Why don't you check your email a little closer.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_f2a4df5e", "Good idea! Thanks.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_f3ec92a", "Use the planetary map to travel to the vendors listed on it, but not all vendors will be listed there. For the unlisted ones, you'll have to travel around looking for player-owned buildings that hold vendors. Once you've found a vendor, double-click it to see what it has for sale. You can also check bazaar terminals, but the listings on those will only be low-end starships and ship components, if even that.");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_f90ad503", "I see. Thanks!");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_fa94d5c5", "Good-bye!");
stringFiles[278].addEntry("s_fd5402d8", "Ah! Then it should give you information about where to go to start your naval adventure. Good luck, my friend!");

stringFiles[279] = new StringFile("conversation/greeter_theed_protocol_droid");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("do_not_edit", "The English version of this file (greeter_theed_protocol_droid) is automatically generated by the SwgConversationEditor.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_0", "");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_12157feb", "The military gives out free ships?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_144ec5cc", "Sounds good. Thanks!");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_17bc5d9b", "When you approach the space station, use SHIFT+C to target it and open communication with the commander. You will be asked if you want to purchase repairs or if you want to land on the planet.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_1bb82d7c", "I bid you hello. As you are a pilot, I would be happy to record any stories of your journeys in space so that I may replay them later for my master here. He speaks only the language of the Mon Calamari, so I will later translate for him.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_2124eaf5", "I bid you hello. Master Woodle was once a captain on a freighter, but he is now retired. If I can answer any questions that might help you become a pilot, it would be my pleasure. Master Woodle is the true expert on space flight, but he only speaks Mon Calamari. Therefore I shall speak with you.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_21bf1a8c", "How do I join the Alliance?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_2318bee", "On the lower right-hand side of your screen should be a 'letter' icon that is flashing. Double-click on this icon, and it will bring up your personal email. Read over the subject and sender, and scroll through the body text to get all the details.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_270c87b2", "How do I get them to repair my ship?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_27186cee", "I don't have enough money.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_29894b97", "I don't know how to check.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_3059f369", "What then?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_32146025", "Then what?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_472f61d1", "Local space stations are the easiest way to get your ship repaired. When you are heading back here, you should stop at the space station and ask them for repairs. They will provide a quick estimate on what it will take to get you back on track.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_495777c0", "Have you checked any vendors? Merchants use vendors to help sell their merchandise. Shipwrights put finished starships and ship components for sale on their vendors, and then you can go to those vendors and purchase what you need.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_52939a0", "How do I check my email?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_558a361a", "The Imperial Navy? I've heard that they are sending out recruitment emails to everyone they can locate these days. Have you checked your email today?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_5618d2cd", "No. I have received no email.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_5989c487", "There are all sorts of civilian contracts available on the 'mission terminals' you find throughout town. Look for them near any major structure. Use the terminal to bring up the current list of local contracts. Choose the one that interests you most and you'll make money when the task is complete.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_59c0790e", "I don't have any questions.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_5b893f7c", "It does.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_5e410744", "Right-click on the map location to create and activate a waypoint. Follow the waypoint to the trainer's location.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_66cf154b", "Very good, sir. Are you certain you had no other questions?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_6840bfa2", "Double-click on the envelope icon, and read your mail!Do you have any other questions?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_68cb68ff", "Is there anyone else I could fly for?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_71e7bd4f", "Strange. Seems that if they undertook the risk to send you a message, they would make it clear how to respond. Why don't you check your email a bit more carefully.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_72df796a", "Good luck with that. I don't want to get too close to the Galactic Civil War, myself.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_82519d76", "Things are tough all over during this Galactic Civil War. A lot of pilots are flying for either the Empire or the Rebellion these days. Ever think of joining the military to get a starship?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_8515e448", "Yes. I have an email from the Imperial Navy.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_8b23fac", "I want to learn to fly.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_8b37a99a", "How do I make money?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_8cf9be64", "Where can I find a vendor?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_93280d8a", "Good idea. Thanks!");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_9f7f7c0a", "I think that the majority of pilot trainers are registered with the planetary map. Try opening the planetary map with CTRL+V. On the right-hand side, there is a listing of categories. Look under 'trainer' to find any local pilot teacher who's looking for pupils.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_a0546c2a", "That's what I hear. Or something like that anyway. The Empire's pretty well-equipped and can't really have much of a navy if their pilots don't have ships. I've also heard rumors that the Alliance has a fleet of ships available for new recruits.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_a9850aec", "I got an email from the Alliance!");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_abc6d2f6", "Your best bet is to get in touch with the Empire and sign up for their training program. There are others who will urge you to put your efforts to use in the Alliance, but fools will be fools.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_acc368b1", "How do I join the Empire?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_add31f19", "I need a starship.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_b0b2621a", "It doesn't");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_b641cda6", "Where can I find a bazaar terminal?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_b9b27823", "Thank you.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_ba3c26af", "You did? These are desperate times, indeed. The email should probably indicate where you are supposed to go for initial recruitment.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_ba95f774", "Bazaar terminals are located all over major cities. Check the areas surrounding major hot spots like the starport, the bank, any of the cantinas, or even the hospitals.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_c2db6878", "Good-bye.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_c4682ea6", "Thanks!");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_c890dd97", "As you wish. Any other questions?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_c9e97ed5", "How else would I join up?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_cb747ceb", "Hmm. Me neither. Maybe you should give it a little time?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_cdb17e79", "How do I check the planetary map?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_cf5fc0f", "How do I repair my starship?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_d9231b4f", "There are freelance pilots working in most systems. Some are CorSec pilots, others are part of the RSF of Naboo, and of course, others are smugglers or pirates. I wouldn't recommend those last two if you want to pursue a lengthy career, but, at the same time, some of the best military pilots I know were once smugglers. Most freelance organizations will send recruitment emails. You might try checking your email for something like that.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_da08c873", "That's sort of tricky. There may be some Alliance pilots bold enough to register their locations on the planetary map. Have you looked at the planetary map yet?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_dfef4e2f", "As you wish. Do you have any other questions?");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_e013f498", "Look for the flashing 'envelope' icon on your interface. It's placed on the lower right-hand side of your screen by default.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_e4004503", "Very well. Thank you.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_e843e3ab", "Use the command CTRL+V to open the planetary map. On the right side of your display, you will see a listing of trainers by category. All local trainers who register with the planet will appear on this list. Click the 'Trainer' tab and then look for a pilot trainer.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_f2a4df5e", "Good idea! Thanks.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_f3ec92a", "Use the planetary map to travel to the vendors listed on it, but not all vendors will be listed there. For the unlisted ones, you'll have to travel around looking for player-owned buildings that hold vendors. Once you've found a vendor, double-click it to see what it has for sale. You can also check bazaar terminals, but the listings on those will only be low-end starships and ship components, if even that.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_f90ad503", "I see. Thanks!");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_fa68600d", "I bid you hello. As you are not a pilot and have no means to become one, I'm afraid our conversation is at an end.");
stringFiles[279].addEntry("s_fd5402d8", "Ah! Then it should give you information about where to go to start your naval adventure. Good luck, my friend!");

stringFiles[280] = new StringFile("conversation/greeter_tyrena_disgraced_corsec");
stringFiles[280].addEntry("do_not_edit", "The English version of this file (greeter_tyrena_disgraced_corsec) is automatically generated by the SwgConversationEditor.");
stringFiles[280].addEntry("s_0", "");
stringFiles[280].addEntry("s_191802ec", "There's no money to give back! Like I said, I've already ordered the fountain and that includes paying for it. I no longer have the money.");
stringFiles[280].addEntry("s_1fb826e9", "Because an Imperial investigator decided to look into it and now claims that it was all a fraud. And that I've kept the money for myself. But I haven't! I ordered the fountain. It should be here any day now. That's even why I rented this load-carrying droid. Just waiting now for the fountain to arrive. I hope it's not much longer.");
stringFiles[280].addEntry("s_1fd2fde4", "Sounds like a nice idea. Why are you so worried?");
stringFiles[280].addEntry("s_39b9ae7", "Sounds like a pretty bad situation.");
stringFiles[280].addEntry("s_3f9656b2", "You could not be more correct. That investigator seems to be out for blood. My friend here, Larek, thinks we should just leave the planet and hide out. Maybe join the Rebellion. But I really shouldn't be saying that. The fountain is on the way. It'll be here. It has to.");
stringFiles[280].addEntry("s_5071a40b", "Maybe you should just give all the money back?");
stringFiles[280].addEntry("s_5ff8baab", "I was wondering if you could answer some questions?");
stringFiles[280].addEntry("s_61113bf6", "What am I gonna do? What am I gonna do? Where is that fountain? That stupid fountain.");
stringFiles[280].addEntry("s_86e4bf6f", "Look, I've got a lot on my mind right now. Sorry to be a bit cross, but you are of no interest to me. If you were to take an interest in space flight, we might have something to talk about. But not until then.");
stringFiles[280].addEntry("s_8dd47fdc", "Could I ask you some questions?");
stringFiles[280].addEntry("s_99f73b4f", "Oh, hello. Don't worry. That fountain is on the way. Those donations are being put to good use exactly as promised. If you see that Imperial investigator, tell him it's on the way, okay? It really is.");
stringFiles[280].addEntry("s_9f080930", "Oh, it's a fountain I raised money for. I wanted to do something for the community here in Tyrena. There's a big empty plaza over near the Agrilat Geyser. I thought it would be nice to have a fountain there. So I asked for donations to raise money for one.");
stringFiles[280].addEntry("s_dd05928", "What fountain?");
stringFiles[280].addEntry("s_ec947daf", "I'm kind of frazzled at the moment. Can't really concentrate on anything. You should ask my friend here, Larek. He's a pilot. He knows things.");

