stringFiles[953] = new StringFile("newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_1_reply_1", "What did you do to my ship?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_1_reply_2", "What is this terminal for?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_1_reply_3", "Bank?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_1_reply_4", "Item dispenser?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_1_start", "Well it seems your ship wasn't carrying contraband after all.  Pity we didn't discover that sooner...");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_2_bank_answer", "You don't need cash on hand to buy things.  You can purchase items from the commodities market on any planet, and the credits will be deducted from your bank automatically.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_2_bank_question", "What if I want to buy something?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_2_explain", "Don't worry!  We've taken care of everything.  We've given you more than enough credits to reimburse you for your loss.  You can deposit them at this banking terminal.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_2_explain_2", "When you get to a planet, look for a commodities market and buy anything you might possibly need.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_2_explain_bank", "Once we realized you were innocent, we reimbursed you with a generous number of credits for the destruction of your gear.  You can deposit them in this bank terminal.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_2_explain_terminals", "For your convenience, we'll allow you to access this starport's bank terminal.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_2_more", "I'm afraid not.  It seems your ship was badly damaged and most of your possessions were destroyed.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_2_more_bank", "You should definitely use the bank's safety deposit feature to keep your items safe from harm. It's also a good idea to deposit your credits into your bank accout before shopping at the commodities market since the market deducts credits from your bank account for all purchases.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_2_reply_1", "Can I get back on board the transport now?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_2_reply_2", "What am I supposed to do now?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_2_reply_3", "What about my supplies and equipment?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_2_start", "Well we suspected you were smuggling, so we boarded the transport you were travelling aboard, of course.  Don't worry, we've cleared you of all charges.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_bank_answer_2", "Any items you store in this bank will be transferred to your new bank.  Once you get to your planet, join any bank there and we'll send these items along.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_bank_question_2", "Can I store items in the bank?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_bank_reply_1", "Why should I bank?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_bazaar_1", "Once you've deposited your money at the bank terminal, browse the Item Dispenser to see if there is any equipment you'd like to purchase.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_bazaar_2", "I think The Empire is being more than generous.  Do you know how much it cost us to capture the transport you were on, kill the crew, search for secret cargo holds... not to mention pulling you out of the fire!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_bazaar_3", "Ah, but now, how were we supposed to know that without capturing the transport first?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_bazaar_reply_1", "You didn't give me very much money.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_bazaar_reply_2", "But that transport wasn't smuggling anything!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("banker_greeting", "Well hello!  Come talk to me if you need assistance with this terminal");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("celeb_guy1", "I can't believe that crazy pirate is dead.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("celeb_guy2", "That must have been a tough battle.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("celeb_guy3", "I'm sure glad that's over with.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("celeb_guy4", "Good thing someone came along to kill that pirate.  We'd have been trapped in here forever.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("celeb_guy5", "I hate pirates.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("clone_greeting", "Well hello!  Please allow me to answer any questions that you might have.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("clone_prompt_convo", "Remember, to speak to me just click-and-hold on me until you get the radial menu, then select the CONVERSE menu option.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_1_agree", "There's nothing to it.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_1_explain", "They weren't civilians.  They were dissidents.  Officially, anyway. Now, go get your free supplies from this drum right here, courtesy of the generosity of the Empire.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_1_more", "You people, you're all the same. Look, you were on a ship with dubious credentials. The Star Destroyer hailed you, and you didn't stop fast enough. So they boarded, and brought the survivors over here.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_1_reply_1", "What happened?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_1_reply_2", "What supplies?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_1_reply_3", "The survivors?  You mean the Empire killed civilian passengers?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_1_start", "That's more like it.  Well, I'm your supply disbursement officer.  I don't see why we should waste good supplies on refugees like you.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_1_stuff", "There's some stuff left that the other refugees didn't take. Not much though. In the drum right here.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_2_cloning", "If something should happen to you, your clone will take over with all the skills you had at the time you died.  Though you always have the option to respawn at the nearest cloning facility, unless you've cloned there you will emerge with many, many wounds.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_2_cloning_2", "You should clone yourself whenever you want the option to emerge from that particular location. Otherwise you will appear at the closest cloning facility from where you died, with many wounds. You will also need to set a new cloning location when you travel to a new planet, because there is no interplanetary cloning.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_2_cloning_3", "No.  Only when you want to have the option of appearing at a particular location without a lot of wounds, regardless of where you died.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_2_insurance", "Insurance is a way of better preserving the condition of your belongings in the event of your untimely demise.  The return of nominally damaged, insured items to a cloning facility fetches a much higher price with the facility at which you choose to clone since you subsidize their item retrieval programs by purchasing insurance.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_2_insurance_2", "Your items will suffer a significantly increased decay rate when transported back to your clone. People like to be paid, and cloning facilities don't pay much for recovery of uninsured items; so it stands to reason that uninsured items tend to not be cared for as well as their insured counterparts.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_2_insurance_3", "You must like living life on the edge.... or you like travelling.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_2_insurance_4", "I don't blame you.  It sounds like a real chore.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_2_insurance_5", "Yes!  Insurance is only valid one time.  If you want your items returned to you in a condition similar to last you saw them, you'll have to insure the item again!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_2_reply_1", "Cloning");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_2_reply_2", "Insurance.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_2_reply_3", "How often should I clone?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_2_reply_4", "What happens to uninsured items?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_2_reply_5", "Do I need to clone again every time I die?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_2_reply_6", "Running back to my corpse sounds like fun!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_2_reply_7", "I hate the idea of running to my corpse!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_2_reply_8", "Do I have to insure my items every time I die?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_2_start", "I'm here to explain Cloning and Insurance.  Where would you like to begin?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_3_explain_terminal_1", "Use terminals like this one, located in cloning facilities, to store your clone data.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_3_explain_terminal_2", "I also have an insurance terminal for you here, where you may insure your items to prevent loss.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_4_end", "Sure, whatever.  Look, I think I'll stand guard from the other side of the room, Ok?  And whatever you do, don't get this maniac angry!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_4_explain_1", "Uh huh.  Look, y-you look pretty capable.  C-could you take a peek and see if there are any survivors in the hallway?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_4_explain_2", "The only way through is here.  Past... him.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_4_explain_3", "I, uh, need to stand guard.  In case reinforcements come.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_4_repeat", "What are you doing here?  Get a move on.  I'm, uh, still guarding here.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_4_reply_1", "Calm down, I'm sure that everything will be under control soon.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_4_reply_2", "So how do I get out of here?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_4_reply_3", "Why don't you go?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_4_reply_4", "Sure, I'll check for survivors.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_4_reply_5", "Then I guess I have to go that way.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_4_reply_6", "Sure, I'll check for survivors.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_4_reply_7", "Thank you.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_4_start", "Y-you can't go IN there.  He cut them to pieces!  He's crazy...!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("convo_4_weapon_1", "Wait, you'll need a weapon.  Uh, this is against regs, but... look, just don't tell anyone.  Here.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("darn_empire", "The empire has ruined us!  We had our life savings on that transport!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("explain_lookat", "Well, I have things for you, but I won't give you the time of day unless you actually converse with me.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("good_job", "Good job with that pirate, but what are you doing back here?  Go back through the big room where the pirate was.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("greeter1_bark1", "Ah, I see we have another refugee from the freighter.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("greeter1_bark2", "Well, you're one of the lucky ones.  Most passengers didn't survive.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("greeter1_bark3", "You should know better than to take passage with criminals.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("greeting", "A straggler, eh?  Don't be shy, come on forward.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("ins_user_bark_1", "There's a crazy criminal on the loose!  I hope you've insured your items!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("ins_user_bark_2", "All my items are insured... are yours?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("ins_user_bark_3", "It's a dangerous world.  I'm sure glad there's an insurance terminal right here.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("leave_me_alone", "Oh leave me alone!   I've lost everything!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("mission_1_reply_1", "Where is the Quartermaster?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("mission_1_reply_2", "Will do!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("mission_1_start", "What took you so long to get here?  The shuttle's ready to leave!  Take these release documents to the Quartermaster and get yourself off my space station.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("mission_1_waypoint", "Here are your release documents.  Now get moving!  The Quartermaster is just down the hall, there.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("mission_hail", "You there.  No time for that now.  I've got something for you to do.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("mission_repeat", "Stop messing around with that terminal and deliver your papers to the Quartermaster!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("nervous_guy1", "You couldn't PAY me to go down that hallway!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("nervous_guy2", "That pirate is crazy!  He blocked up the hallway and threatens anyone that goes near him!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("nervous_guy3", "I bet the Empire will send him to the spice mines on Kessel");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("nervous_guy4", "You can't be thinking of going down that hallway?!  Didn't you hear?  CRAZY PIRATE ON THE LOOSE!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("nervous_guy5", "I wish I could go home...");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("off_1_gotrain", "Well there's someone you should talk to right over there.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("off_1_gotrain2", "Ha ha ha!  I suppose not.  Hey, there's someone right here you should talk to about that.  I bet you could learn something.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("off_1_greeting", "Say... you're still alive!  That's amazing.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("off_1_reply_1", "I'd be even better with a little training.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("off_1_reply_2", "Combat isn't really my thing.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("off_1_start", "Good show, in there.  You're quite resourceful.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("pirate_attack", "I'll kill ya!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("pirate_taunt1", "Come any closer and I'll shoot!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("pirate_taunt2", "You'll never take me alive!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("pirate_taunt3", "Well I bet you weren't expecting.... A GRENADE!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("pirate_taunt4", "What the...?  This grenade is defective!  Oh no!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("quarter_1_go", "You may use the travel terminal here and purchase a ticket to anywhere you want to go.  And don't worry about the cost, the Empire will be picking up the tab on this one.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("quarter_1_go_nochoice", "You may use the travel terminal here and be on your way.  And don't worry about the cost of transportation, the Empire will be picking up the tab on this one.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("quarter_1_reply_1", "Can I leave now?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("quarter_1_reply_2", "Where are you sending me?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("quarter_1_start", "Ah!  I see you have the proper documents there.  I'll just take those from you.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("quarter_greeting", "Finally!  The last of the survivors, I take it?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("quarter_nodocs", "You don't have your release papers?  Well you'd better go get them from the Corporal.  Make it snappy!  Hup!  Hup!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("quarter_wait", "Wait a minute there!  You can't use that travel terminal without the proper authorization.  Do you have your release documents on you?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("refugee1", "They're going to ship us off to the spice mines of Kessel.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("refugee2", "The Emperor has disbanded the Senate, now the Empire can do whatever it wants.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("refugee3", "But we're innocent!  We weren't carrying any contraband.  They attacked us for no reason.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("refugee4", "I never should have left Alderaan... Oh, wait...");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("refugee5", "I told you we couldn't outrun an Imperial Star Destroyer.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("release_docs", "Release Documents");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("shout_panic1", "Aaaaiiiiiii!  We're all gonna die!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("shout_panic2", "Mad pirate on the loose!  He's got a bomb!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("shout_panic3", "Someone DO something!!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("shout_panic4", "Shouldn't you be taking care of that crazy pirate or SOMETHING?!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("trainer_grunt", "Huh?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("trapped_guy1", "I don't understand why you won't give me release documents too...");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("trapped_guy2", "I was going to kill that pirate.  It's not my fault someone beat me to it.");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("trapped_guy3", "So I'll be shipped off to the spice mines?  That's not fair!  I heard someone killed the pirate and you're letting them go!");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("trapped_guy4", "This is an outrage!  I demand my release papers this instant!  Uh... please?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("trapped_guy5", "You destroyed my ship!  Ruined my life!  And now you're refusing to release me!  Who is in charge here?");
stringFiles[953].addEntry("trooper_move_along", "Move along.");

stringFiles[954] = new StringFile("newbie_tutorial/newbie_mail");
stringFiles[954].addEntry("collector_body", "You are using the Star Wars Galaxies Collector's Edition.  This character has a special item which is only available to Collector's Edition Users.");
stringFiles[954].addEntry("collector_subject", "Collector's Edition");
stringFiles[954].addEntry("combat_brawler_body", "A brawler like yourself can earn good money by doing missions for people.  Just ask around to see if anyone has anything they need you to do, or seek out a mission terminal.  Careful not to get in over your head though.");
stringFiles[954].addEntry("combat_brawler_subject", "So you like to hit people");
stringFiles[954].addEntry("combat_marksman_body", "Marksmen are always in demand.  Seek out a mission terminal or just ask around town to see if anyone has anything they need shot.  You're just the person to do it!");
stringFiles[954].addEntry("combat_marksman_subject", "There's no match for a good blaster");
stringFiles[954].addEntry("crafting_artisan_body", "You've got the tools to survey for all the resources you need... except hides!  If you want to advance as an artisan, you'd better make some cash to trade for the hides you'll need.  Then you can buy hides at the commodities market.  Maybe there are some missions you can do to earn some money.  Seek out a mission terminal and begin your career as a crafter.");
stringFiles[954].addEntry("crafting_artisan_subject", "You're going to need some money!");
stringFiles[954].addEntry("outdoors_scout_body", "Well don't stand around here reading the holonet all day long - get out there and Scout.  Artisans will need the hides that only you can provide, so remember to harvest resources from the creatures and bring their hides back to the commodities market.  You can even earn some money along the way by taking a mission.  Why don't you stop by a mission terminal on your way out of town?");
stringFiles[954].addEntry("outdoors_scout_subject", "Good scouts are hard to come by");
stringFiles[954].addEntry("science_medic_body", "A good medic is hard to come by, so you'll always be in demand.  You can heal people at the local hospital, and there are always plenty of wounded to tend to.  If you don't feel comfortable charging for your services, maybe you should take a mission from the local mission terminal to earn some cash.   You're going to need to buy supplies to heal people, after all.");
stringFiles[954].addEntry("science_medic_subject", "There are injured people that need your attention!");
stringFiles[954].addEntry("social_entertainer_body", "After a hard day's work everyone needs a chance to relax and unwind... and you're just the person they need to see.  Your services will always be in demand at the local cantina, and if you don't like working for tips then you could seek out a mission from the local mission board.  You might even find a mission custom-tailored for a person of your obvious talent!");
stringFiles[954].addEntry("social_entertainer_subject", "Local Cantina Seeks Entertainer");
stringFiles[954].addEntry("welcome_body", "You have taken your first steps into the immense universe of Star Wars. This game mail is meant to give you a quick welcome and overview. If you need additional details on anything about the game, don't be afraid to bring up the Holocron (default: CTRL H). It offers easy-to-navigate chapters that not only teach you the game, but also gives you starting missions.Unlike many other games, there is no 'one' way to play Star Wars Galaxies. You will be able to live in and interact with the Star Wars universe in a way you never have been able to before.If you are looking for a little direction to get started, we recommend finding a local mission terminal to take some missions. After making some credits doing simple delivery or destroy missions, you may want to start upgrading your equipment. Eventually, you'll want to converse with non-player characters to find more interesting and lucrative missions or you may want to head to the adventure Theme Parks like Jabba's Palace on Tatooine.After that, you goals are largely determined by what you are interested in. For example, you may want to join the Rebellion or Empire and work your way up through the military ranks. You may wish to master multiple professions and become renown throughout the galaxy for your skills. You may want to acquire, make, or sell the best equipment in the galaxy. You might want to explore the ten worlds and find a perfect spot to build your home. You may even want to try to unlock the secret to opening a second character slot that is Force-sensitive (warning: this is extremely difficult, mysterious and dangerous). The choice is really up to you. Your best source for in-depth information on the game will come from other players. You can find players who are ready and willing to answer your questions right now by typing /who newbiehelper. Simply pick one off the list in your chat window and send your question by typing: /tell [player name] I'm new, could you please help me?As a final note, the game is designed around the recommended default Star Wars Galaxies controls. However if you are more comfortable with a different control set up (EQ style, FPS style or Isometric style), you can quickly remap the entire keyboard layout in the Option menus (default CTRL ) - Controls tab - Keymap button - use the dropdown menu).On behalf of the entire development team, thank you and enjoy your time in Star Wars Galaxies. May the Force be with you.");
stringFiles[954].addEntry("welcome_subject", "Welcome to Star Wars Galaxies");

stringFiles[955] = new StringFile("newbie_tutorial/system_messages");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("bank_flytext", "*Access the bank here!*");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("bank_info_1", "Banks let you deposit and withdraw cash on hand.  You can also use the bank to store items.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("bank_info_2", "You can only retrieve your items from the bank in which you stored the item.  You can only store items in the bank you've joined.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("bank_info_3", "Although you can change banks at any time, you can only be a member of one bank at a time.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("bank_info_4", "You can spend credits from your bank account at most terminals.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("bank_info_5", "When you find hard credits (cash on hand), be sure to deposit them in your bank as soon as possible to avoid losing them.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("bazaar_flytext", "*Shop!*");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("bazaar_info_1", "This is an item dispenser.  You can use it to buy basic items in the game.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("bazaar_info_2", "In addition to the basic item dispensers, you'll find a number of terminals that will connect you to the galactic bazaar.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("bazaar_info_3", "Everything from large quantities of resources, to specialized items can be bought and sold at the bazaar terminal.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("chatprompt", "Go ahead and try it.  Just type what you want to say and then press ENTER.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("chatwindow", "This is your chat window.  Type here to speak to your fellow players.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("choose_destination", "Please select a destination from the sub-menu.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("clone_here", "*Clone!*");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("close_inventory", "Press CTRL-I again to close your inventory window.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("close_status_prompt", "Press CTRL-C again to toggle your character status screen off.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("declare_cloned", "Your clone data has been saved!");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("declare_insured", "All of your items have been insured!");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("droid_name", "Q-3PO");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("explain_alt_key", "Press the ALT key to toggle free-mouse mode on and off.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("explain_combat_1", "In combat, you can spend your HEALTH, MIND or ACTION pools to invoke special attacks.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("explain_combat_2", "The ATTACK option on the radial menu will be the default attack for hostile creatures.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("explain_combat_3", "You can attack hostile creatures simply by double-clicking them.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("explain_freemouse", "Notice that your mouse mode changed when you opened that container.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("explain_freemouse_toggle", "You can toggle the mouse mode yourself with the ALT key.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("explain_inventory", "You can examine your inventory by pressing CTRL-I.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("explain_item_used", "You used the item on yourself.  Food will help increase your attributes.  Medicine will help you recover damage to your attributes.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("holocube", "This is your Holocron.  You can access it by pressing CTRL-H.  Whenever you need information about something in Star Wars Galaxies, press CTRL-H to find it in your Holocron.  To close this screen, press CTRL-H again.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("imp_name", "Imperial Officer");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("insure_here", "*Insurance!*");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("keymap", "Star Wars Galaxies contains a variety of different keyboard layouts as well as the ability to remap keys.  After you arrive at your starting planet, access the Options menu by hitting  CTRL-O, select the Controls option and then the Keymap option.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("lookaround", "You can look around by moving your mouse.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("loot_pirate", "Congratulations!  The pirate has been destroyed.  Now you can loot his corpse by clicking and holding your mouse on him until you get the radial menu option to LOOT.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("make_promise", "To swear your oath, please type the words I PROMISE into your chat window, and press ENTER.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("menu_corellia", "Corellia");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("menu_naboo", "Naboo");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("menu_tatooine", "Tatooine");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("menu_travel", "DESTINATION");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("mission_terminal", "You cannot take a mission from this terminal.  To take a mission, you will need to find a mission terminal on a planet.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("mousewheel", "Using the mouse-wheel, scroll forward to zoom into your character.  Notice that if you zoom in all the way, you'll be in first-person mode.  Scroll backwards to zoom-out of your character, and into third-person mode.  You can also zoom your camera in and out by pressing the keypad plus and minus keys.  Try zooming between 1st and 3rd person.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("mousewheel_repeat", "Give it a try.  Scroll out to 3rd-person and take a look at yourself.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("movement_keyboard", "Use the arrow keys to move.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("movement_mouse", "Or hold down the right mouse-button to move forward.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("move_to_cloning", "Take the elevator down and visit our state-of-the-art cloning facility.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("move_to_item_room", "Excellent!  Come through the door and down the hallway there.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("move_to_toolbar", "Move a food item from your inventory to a blank slot on your toolbar.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("newbie_mail", "You've received a message.  Press the letter-icon on  your button bar to access your email!");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("oath_explain", "You are required to promise to obey the code of conduct and to treat your fellow players with respect, before moving on.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("open_me", "*Open Me!*");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("open_status_prompt", "Good job.  Now I want you to look at your character status screen.  Press CTRL-C.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("part_1", "PART ONE OF NINE (movement and chat)");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("part_10", "PART TEN OF ELEVEN");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("part_11", "PART ELEVEN OF ELEVEN");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("part_2", "PART TWO OF NINE (conversing with npcs and inventory)");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("part_3", "PART THREE OF NINE (banking and shopping)");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("part_4", "PART FOUR OF NINE (cloning and insurance)");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("part_5", "PART FIVE OF NINE (combat moves and radar)");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("part_6", "PART SIX OF NINE (combat)");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("part_7", "PART SEVEN OF NINE (skill training)");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("part_8", "PART EIGHT OF NINE (missions and waypoints)");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("part_9", "PART NINE OF NINE (bye!)");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("pickup_complete", "You've put the item in your inventory.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("prompt_choose_open", "Great!  Now select the Open option to access the contents of the container.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("prompt_find_food", "Scroll through your inventory until you locate one of the food items that you've just picked-up.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("prompt_open_box", "To open the box just click and hold until you see the radial menu appear.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("prompt_select_pickup", "Now choose the Pick Up option to move the item to your inventory.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("prompt_take_items", "You can take these items by clicking-and-holding until you get the radial menu option on each item.  Pick up all of the items, and then click the X in the upper-right-hand corner of the container to close the box.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("prompt_use_item", "Select the Use option to use this item.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("quarter_name", "The Quartermaster");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("radar", "If you're going down that hallway, you might want advanced warning of what's down there.  This is your radar.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("radar_more", "The red dots show potentially aggressive entities.  Yellow dots indicate peaceful life signatures.  You can also access an overlay map with CTRL-M.  Press CTRL-M again to turn it off.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("receive_weapon", "A weapon has been added to your inventory.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("release_docs", "Release Documents");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("repeatchatprompt", "Don't be shy.  Type something in your chatwindow and press Enter.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("repeat_closestatus_prompt", "Now press CTRL-C again to close your character status screen.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("repeat_item_room_prompt", "Come on.  Don't keep me waiting all day.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("repeat_open_box", "You might find something in the box you need.  Click and hold your mouse-button down on the box until you see the radial menu.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("repeat_open_inventory", "Press CTRL-I to open your inventory, and select one of the food items you found in the crate.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("repeat_status_prompt", "Press CTRL-C to view your character status screen.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("repeat_visit_commerce", "No need to stick around here all day.  Walk down the corridor to the next area.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("select_dest", "Select your destination by clicking on one of the planets on the screen.  When you have selected the planet, select which city you wish to travel to by clicking on the picture to the right of the screen.  When you are ready to travel to the city, click on the arrow in the lower right-hand corner of the screen.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("show_toolbar", "This is your toolbar.  You can put things on it for instant access.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("start_loc", "Starting Location");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("stat_migration", "Although your stats have been optimized for your starting profession, you may wish to change your stats in order to pursue a different profession, either instead of or in addition to your starting profession.  Once you are in the world, stat migration is a slow process:  Gradually moving points from one stat to another.  However, in this Planet Selection Room, you may migrate your stats and the changes will take effect immediately.  If you would like to change your stats now, press CTRL-C and choose the Stat Migration button.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("stat_open", "Although your stats have been optimized for your starting profession, you may wish to change your stats in order to pursue a different profession, either instead of or in addition to your starting profession.  Once you are in the world, stat migration is a slow progress:  Gradually moving points from one stat to another.  However, in this Tutorial, you may migrate your stats and the changes will take effect immediately.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("swear_reminder", "You cannot become a citizen of Star Wars Galaxies until you promise to abide by the code of conduct.  To swear your oath, type I PROMISE into the chat window and hit the ENTER key.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("the_oath", "I promise to treat my fellow players and citizens with respect and to obey the code of conduct");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("the_promise", "I promise");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_00_toolbardrag", "You can drag items into your toolbar for easy access.  Simply click on the item and then drag it to an open slot on your toolbar.  Press the corresponding function key to use the item.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_08", "Move forward and click-and-hold your mouse on the Imperial Officer until the radial menu appears.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_09", "He is now your look-at target.  His name appears over his head.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_10", "Click and hold the mouse button to get  a radial menu on the Imperial Officer.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_11", "Do you see the option to converse?  While holding your mouse button, move to the converse option and let go of the mouse button to select it.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_12", "Now you're in a conversation.  You can choose one of the responses to the right with your mouse.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_13", "Remember, you don't speak to other players this way.  Just type to talk to other players.  When you are finished conversing with the Imperial Officer, select the STOP CONVERSING option.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_28", "Converse with the Imperial Officer");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_32", "Banks let you deposit and withdraw cash on hand.  You can also use the bank to store items.  You can only retrieve your items from the bank in which you stored the item.  You can only store items in the bank you've joined.  Although you can change banks at any time, you can only be a member of one bank at a time.  You can spend credits from your bank account at most terminals.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_33", "When you find hard credits (cash on hand) be sure to deposit them in your bank as soon as possible to avoid losing them.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_36", "Move down the ramp toward the cloning and insurance terminals.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_37", "Use the cloning terminal.  You can do this through the radial menu, or you can just double-click.  The cursor changes when over a usable item.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_38", "Use the insurance terminal.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_40", "Converse with the soldier.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_43", "You can zoom the overlay map using the mousewheel, while holding down the CTRL key.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_44_attacking", "When you hover your cursor over someone, your cursor changes to let you know that you can attack them.  Double-clicking them will attack them.  You can also cycle through targets with the tab key.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_45", "The hallway is blocked by debris.  Attack it to destroy it.  Then proceed to the next room to face your enemy.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_49", "The Imperial Officer has directed you to a Skill Trainer.  Converse with the Skill Trainer to learn your first skill.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_50", "You've picked up your first skill.  There are many skills to master in your chosen profession and there are advanced professions that only open up once you have mastered many skills.  You can check your skills using the skills window.  You can reach this with the skills button on the button bar, or by pressing CTRL-S.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_51", "You can also check your character status after your fight, by pressing the character-sheet button on the button bar, or CTRL-C.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_53", "Mission terminals like those to your left are located throughout the world.  Whenever you want a quick adventure you can always take a job from a mission terminal.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_54", "You can also speak to npcs and do tasks for them.  There's one over there who has something for you to do.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_55_waypoints", "Waypoints indicate destinations.  When you have a job or mission, you can follow the waypoint on your radar.  They appear light blue.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_56", "Move to the next room to deliver your release documents to the Quartermaster.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_57", "Converse with the Quartermaster.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("tut_60", "Thank you.  You are now a citizen of Star Wars Galaxies.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("use_toolbar", "To use the item on your toolbar, press the function-key which corresponds with the toolbar slot.  F1 is the first slot.  F12 is the last slot.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("visit_commerce_room", "Proceed to the next room.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("waypoint", "Waypoint");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("welcome", "Welcome to Star Wars Galaxies.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("wrong_bank", "You cannot use this bank terminal.  Use the bank terminal in the middle of the room.");
stringFiles[955].addEntry("yoink", "*Yoink!*");

stringFiles[956] = new StringFile("new_player");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("artisan_added", "[beep... boop... whir] You have joined the Artisan profession. I have downloaded some Artisan tasks so that you may learn more about being an Artisan.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("artisan_quest_00", "[beep... tweet... whir] Are you ready to learn more about the Artisan profession? I've downloaded some Artisan tasks that will help.Ready to begin?");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("artisan_quest_01", "[tweet... boop... blip] As an Artisan, you will need various resources to craft your goods. As someone new to the profession, your best method for finding these resources will be to survey for them. Your first task is to survey for any type of mineral.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("artisan_quest_02", "[bweepo...zeek... beep] Now that you have found some minerals in the area, take some resource samples. Continue until you have 8 units of a single type of mineral.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("artisan_quest_03", "[zzt... bweeo... boop...razzle] For your next task, survey for and sample a metal. Any type will do, but you must find 19 units of the same type of metal to complete this task in addition to the 8 units of minerals you collected previously.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("artisan_quest_04", "[blip... bweep... dadeep] Now you have the resources required to craft a chemical survey device. Make one of them.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("artisan_quest_05", "[boop... clik... bweep... bzzt] I have downloaded a service contract that you should now be able to fulfill. A guild of hunters wishes to present a demonstration on basic rifle craftsmanship. The contract asks that you craft some rifles, and I'll record your actions. The guild leaders will then edit together a holovid for their presentation.Use the Artisan knowledge you have gained to gather resources for 5 CDEF rifles and craft them. If you wish, you may craft these in practice mode so that you do not clutter your inventory with surplus rifles.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("artisan_quest_05_b", "Rifles Crafted: ");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("artisan_quest_complete", "[beep... clik... beep... whir... blip] Congratulations on finishing the tasks for the Artisan profession. Continue using what you have learned to progress in this profession. Well done and happy journeys.If you'd like to try any of the other starting professions (Brawler, Marksman, Scout, Medic, or Entertainer), simply speak to a trainer for the profession you wish to try and tell them you are interested in learning that profession. And don't worry... I can help you with those professions as well.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("brawler_added", "[beep... freetle... boop... whir] You have joined the Brawler profession. I have downloaded some Brawler tasks so that you may learn more about being a Brawler.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("brawler_berserk", "[whir... clik... beep... tweetle... razz]While Berserk, you cause more melee damage to your targets but get hit more often in return.To go Berserk, type /berserk1 or you may drag Berserk 1 from the Other tab of your Command Browser (CTRL-A) to your hotkey bar at the top of your screen and use the corresponding hotkey or click on it directly.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("brawler_center_of_being", "[whir... clik... bleet... zzt... tweet]When using Center of Being, your character will focus on avoiding combat blows.To use Center of Being, type /centerofbeing or you may drag Center of Being from the Other tab in your Command Browser (CTRL-A) to your hotkey bar at the top of your screen and use the corresponding hotkey or click on it directly.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("brawler_lunge", "[whir... clik... bweep... freet... blip]A Lunge attack can slightly extend your range, and has a chance to lower the posture of your target... possibly limiting their ability to attack or defend.To use Lunge, you will need to type the command that goes with your style of attack:     For one-handed weapons, type /melee1hlunge1 <target>    For two-handed weapons, type /melee2hlunge1 <target>    For polearm weapons, type /polearmlunge1 <target>    For unarmed, type /unarmedlunge1 <target>If you have your target selected, you can leave off the <target> part of the command.Or you may drag the appropriate Lunge 1 command from the Combat tab of your Command Browser (CTRL-A) to your hotkey bar at the top of your screen and use the corresponding hotkey or click on it directly.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("brawler_quest_00", "[beep... clik... boop... whir] Are you ready to learn more about the Brawler profession? I've downloaded some Brawler tasks that will help.Ready to begin?");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("brawler_quest_01", "[beep... blip... zeek... boweep... clik] As one who has chosen the Brawler approach to combat, you may wish to choose a style of melee fighting that suits you. The four primary approaches to melee combat are unarmed, the use of one-handed weapons, the use of two-handed weapons, and the use of polearm weapons. Unarmed combat, of course, doesn't involve using a weapon. Basic weapons for the others are a survival knife (a one-handed weapon), a heavy axe (a two-handed weapon), and a wood staff (a polearm weapon). Which weapon would you like to use?");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("brawler_quest_02", "[zwing... bleep... vwoot... whir] The primary aim of a Brawler is victory in combat, and it's time to begin working toward that. Your first task is to go to kill a creature. You'll find some on the outskirts of this city. Kill any one creature you find to complete this task.Be sure to equip your weapon in order to use it in combat... unless, of course, you wish to fight unarmed. To equip a weapon, simply double-click it in your inventory. You can also use the radial menu on the weapon and choose Equip.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("brawler_quest_03", "[dadeep... blip... boop... boop] You have special abilities that can aid you while fighting. The Berserk ability increases the damage you do in combat though you become a bit easier for your opponent to hit. Use Berserk while fighting and killing a creature.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("brawler_quest_04", "[bweep... tweet... bweeo... zzt] Using a Lunge can extend your range a small amount, but more importantly it can change the posture of your target. This can render them helpless and often unable to attack until they recover. Use Lunge while fighting and killing a creature.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("brawler_quest_05", "[vwoot... beep... blip... boop]Using Center of Being can provide you a defensive bonus by helping you avoid being hit by your opponent. Use Center of Being while fighting and killing a creature.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("brawler_quest_06", "[beep... whir... tweetle... whir... clik]I have downloaded a job with a more substantial payment. A local scholar would like to study the stresses of combat on one such as yourself who is still new to the art of melee battle. He requires that you find and kill 10 creatures. I shall record your actions and transmit the recordings to him when you've completed this task.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("brawler_quest_06_b", "Creatures Killed: ");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("brawler_quest_complete", "[beep... whir... clik... tweetle... bweep] Congratulations on finishing the tasks for the Brawler profession. Continue using what you have learned to progress in this profession. Well done and happy journeys.If you'd like to try any of the other starting professions (Marksman, Scout, Medic, Artisan, or Entertainer), simply speak to a trainer for the profession you wish to try and tell them you are interested in learning that profession. And don't worry... I can help you with those professions as well.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("brawler_quest_weapon_choice", "[beep... blip... zeek... boweep... clik] As one who has chosen the Brawler approach to combat, you may wish to choose a style of melee fighting that suits you. The four primary approaches to melee combat are unarmed, the use of one-handed weapons, the use of two-handed weapons, and the use of polearm weapons. Unarmed combat, of course, doesn't involve using a weapon. Basic weapons for the others are a survival knife (a one-handed weapon), a heavy axe (a two-handed weapon), and a wood staff (a polearm weapon). Which weapon would you like to use?");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("calling_stored_helper_droid", "[zwoop... blip... clik... bweep]When I have been stored, you may call me from my control device in your datapad. Simply open your datapad (CTRL-D) and then select the control device with my name. It will be in the Data tab in your datapad. Click on my control device and use the radial menu choice to Call me.If I'm currently in the world somewhere, instead of a Call menu option, you will see a Store menu option. You can use this choice to store me in my control device.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("cdef_carbine_button", "Carbine");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("cdef_pistol_button", "Pistol");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("cdef_rifle_button", "Rifle");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("completed_first_profession", "Well done! You've completed an entire profession's set of tasks. As a reward, take this vehicle rental. Have fun!");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("completed_first_task", "Congratulations on completing your first ever task! If you wish to celebrate, you can use these fireworks.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("completed_second_task", "Whoo, you're on  roll! Here's an authorization release for any cloning facility... it lets you bind once for free. Enjoy!");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("completed_third_task", "You're doing great! Here's a travel voucher. Use it to get a free shuttleport or spaceport ticket! Wow!");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("continue_button", "Continue");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("counter_not_update", "         (Please note that as you progress in this task,         the counter will not update without being re-opened.)");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("credits_reward", "%DI credits have been deposited into your bank account.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("default_cancel_button", "Cancel");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("default_okay_button", "Okay");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("default_revert_button", "Revert");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("default_text", "Warning... I have nothing to say.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("delayed_accepting_quest", "[boop...bleep..bleep... whir... clik] Very well. When you are ready to begin, simply use my radial menu. When you click on me and the radial menu appears, hover over the menu option labeled Profession Quests and then choose the submenu for the profession about which you are ready to learn.  And remember that I am authorized to reward you for your progress as you complete these tasks.If I'm ever needed but not out by your side, you may call me from my control device in your datapad. Simply open your datapad (CTRL-D) and then select the control device with my name. It will be in the Data tab in your datapad. Click on my control device and use the radial menu choice to Call me.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("droid_greeting_begin_01", "[beep... clik... zwing... bweep... beep] Greetings, ");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("droid_greeting_begin_02", "[bwoop... clik... zwing... bweep... beep] Hello, ");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("droid_greeting_begin_03", "[tweet... clik... zwing... bweep... beep] Salutations, ");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("droid_greeting_end", "I am your helper droid and will be helping you to learn more about any of the Starting Professions you wish to undertake.I have downloaded some tasks to help you get started. Would you like to begin?");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("droid_periodic_check_end", "I am merely checking to see if you might be in need of assistance.If so, you need simply select the profession with which you would like help and then click on the Okay button.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("droid_prompt_end", "and welcome back. I am, as always, at your service.If I may be of assistance, simply select the profession you want and then click on the Okay button.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_added", "[beep... beep... bop] You have joined the Entertainer profession. I have downloaded some Entertainment tasks so that you may learn more about being an Entertainer.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_image_design", "[whir... clik... beep... boop... zweep]Using Image Design allows you to alter the way your character looks, or to alter the way other characters look as long as they are in a group with you and consent to your changes.To Image Design, type /imagedesign <target's name>. You may also simply click on your target to select them and then type /imagedesign. If you aren't targeting anyone, then you will image design yourself.Another way to begin image designing is use the Image Design radial menu choice on a player with whom you are grouped.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_quest_00", "[beep... beep... bop] Are you ready to learn more about the Entertainer profession? I've downloaded some Entertainer tasks that will help.Ready to begin?");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_quest_01", "[whir... bleep... vwoot] Dancing is one of the basic forms of entertainment that you can master as an Entertainer. Please perform any dance.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_quest_02", "[bwoop... tweet... razzle] Another standard form of entertainment at your disposal is the performance of music. Please play any piece of music.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_quest_03_bothan", "[boop... zeet... zwing... clik] Some entertainers choose to follow the path of becoming an Image Designer. Image design can involve many things such as hair styling, body sculpting, and even skin tinting. You next task is to use your image design skills and change your hair to a different style.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_quest_03_human", "[boop... zeet... zwing... clik] Some entertainers choose to follow the path of becoming an Image Designer. Image design can involve many things such as hair styling, body sculpting, and even skin tinting. You next task is to use your image design skills and change your hair to a different style.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_quest_03_ithorian", "[beep... clik... tweetle... clik... whir... zang] Your next task was to restyle your hair, but as an Ithorian, you are not yet able to do this. I have been authorized to skip this step and move on to the next one.Before I do, I'd like to make sure you know that you can help others style their hair by grouping with them, then targeting them, and then either selecting the Image Design radial menu option or typing /imagedesign. If you progress as an Image Designer, you will eventually learn how to change many aspects of your appearance.Let's move on.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_quest_03_moncalamari", "[beep... clik... tweetle... clik... whir... zang] Your next task was to restyle your hair, but as a Mon Calamari, you do not have hair or anything else to style. I have been authorized to skip this step and move on to the next one.Before I do, I'd like to make sure you know that you can help others style their hair by grouping with them, then targeting them, and then either selecting the Image Design radial menu option or typing /imagedesign. If you progress as an Image Designer, you will eventually learn how to change the style and color your skull markings... among other things.Let's move on.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_quest_03_rodian", "[boop... zeet... zwing... clik] Some entertainers choose to follow the path of becoming an Image Designer. Image design can involve many things such as hair styling, body sculpting, and even skin tinting. You next task is to use your image design skills and change your frills to a different style.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_quest_03_sullustan", "[beep... clik... tweetle... clik... whir... zang] Your next task was to restyle your hair, but as a Sullustan, you do not have hair or anything else to style. I have been authorized to skip this step and move on to the next one.Before I do, I'd like to make sure you know that you can help others style their hair by grouping with them, then targeting them, and then either selecting the Image Design radial menu option or typing /imagedesign. If you progress as an Image Designer, you will eventually learn how to change the style and color your skull markings... among other things.Let's move on.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_quest_03_trandoshan", "[boop... zeet... zwing... clik] Some entertainers choose to follow the path of becoming an Image Designer. Image design can involve many things such as hair styling, body sculpting, and even skin tinting. You next task is to use your image design skills and change your skull ridges to a different style.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_quest_03_twilek", "[boop... zeet... zwing... clik] Some entertainers choose to follow the path of becoming an Image Designer. Image design can involve many things such as hair styling, body sculpting, and even skin tinting. You next task is to use your image design skills and change your lekku to a different style.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_quest_03_wookiee", "[beep... clik... tweetle... clik... whir... zang] Your next task was intended to be to restyle your hair, but as a Wookiee, your fur cannot be styled so easily. I have been authorized to skip this step and move on to the next one.Before I do, I'd like to make sure you know that you can help others style their hair by grouping with them, then targeting them, and then either selecting the Image Design radial menu or typing /imagedesign. If you progress as an Image Designer, you will eventually learn how to change your fur color and markings... among other things.Let's move on.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_quest_03_zabrak", "[boop... zeet... zwing... clik] Some entertainers choose to follow the path of becoming an Image Designer. Image design can involve many things such as hair styling, body sculpting, and even skin tinting. You next task is to use your image design skills and change your horn pattern to a different style.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_quest_04", "[beep... dadeet... blip] To enhance your music or dancing, you will need to add flourishes while you perform. This will not only enhance your performance, but it also increases your effectiveness with various entertainer abilities.Please play a song or dance a dance and add flourishes during your performance.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_quest_05", "[bweet... whir... zeet] An Entertainer can relieve Battle Fatigue for other players by performing music or dancing for them. They can only do this in a cantina or in a theater.Find a cantina or theater and go inside.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_quest_06", "[clik... beep... zwing... beep] I have received a request from a local sociologist. She wishes to study the reaction of people to the latest trends in dance and music. Ask another player to either watch you dance or listen to you play music. Do this for a total of 7 players. You may perform for all 7 players at once or each of them individually, but you must entertain all 7 of them using the same type of performance... meaning dance for them or play music, but not both.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_quest_06_b", "Players Entertained: ");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("entertainer_quest_complete", "[beep... zwing... tweet... bweep... beep] Congratulations on finishing the tasks for the Entertainer profession. Continue using what you have learned to progress in this profession. Well done and happy journeys.If you'd like to try any of the other starting professions (Brawler, Marksman, Scout, Medic, or Artisan), simply speak to a trainer for the profession you wish to try and tell them you are interested in learning that profession. And don't worry... I can help you with those professions as well.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("general_combat_button", "Combat");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("general_entertainer_button", "Entertainer Info");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("general_greeting_prose_01", "[beep... clik] Greetings %TO.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("general_greeting_prose_02", "[bwoop... clik] Hello %TO.");
stringFiles[956].addEntry("general_greeting_prose_03", "[tweet... clik] Salutations %TO.");
